  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The whole-model 2D Contour now plans all its bands first and emits them at the end (new module `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_whole_fence.rs`).\n- Before a band is emitted, its lead room (`PreparedBand::room`) is its center region plus a fence around each ring of another band. The fence is 0.05 mm on each side. The fence goes only around a ring that is cut on a level that this band also cuts.\n- The lead fitter then shortens, reseats or refuses a lead that would cross that ring. A refusal gives a named note.\n- The levels do not change. The grown ring still steps down from the stock top. At stock top 18.5 its first pass is Top Z 15, which is one stepdown under the stock top.\n- An error that carries the partial path (ghost) emits the planned bands first. Thus the ghost does not change.\n- `emit_band` reads `band.room` when it is set (`contour.rs`).\n- The decision entry is `docs/decisions/2677-shared-level-lead-fence.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nA grown outline takes the levels above its first level (`reach_up`). These levels can share a plane with a ring of an earlier band. With the stock top one stepdown or more over Top Z, this shared plane is Top Z. A lead longer than the gap between the two rings crossed the other ring at that Z. The verifier's `Crossing` law (`crates/sim/src/verify/crossing.rs`) then blocked the post. The same thing occurs with no stock over Top Z, at the flat levels under Top Z.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Before the fix, the new motion pin gave `[Crossing { moves: [3, 57] }, Crossing { moves: [18, 72] }, Crossing { moves: [33, 87] }]` for the case with no stock.\n- After the fix, the pin gives no warnings for the case with no stock and for stock top 31 (Top Z 25, stepdown 5).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` `contour_whole_new_outline::leads_of_one_outline_do_not_cross_a_grown_outline_on_the_same_level`. This test is new. It fails before the fix and passes after it.\n- `camcraft-app` `contour_whole_step::case1_chamfered_island_top_contours_plate_to_bottom_with_tabs`. This test now also runs stock top 18.5 (oversized and not oversized). It asserts that the post has no blocking warning, that the post is not blocked, and that a pass at Top Z 15 exists and no pass at Z 13.5 exists.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on 7e5e646b2: 124 steps, 0 failed, not VOID.\n  - `camcraft-motion`: 66 steps, 967 passed, 0 failed, 51 ignored.\n  - `camcraft-app`: 58 steps, 550 passed, 0 failed, 12 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- I did not run the pre-fix `contour_whole_step` case at 18.5. The issue report gives that failure.\n- The heavy release lanes did not run.\n- I did not open the GUI.\n- The fence is per band, not per level. A lead of a band on a level that no other band shares can also become shorter at a fenced ring. The decision entry records this.\n- With the deferred emit, the lead notes of a band come after the planning notes of later bands. A planning error of a later band now comes before an emit error of an earlier band.\n- This PR does not change #2672, #2673 or #2674.\n\nChangelog: Whole-model 2D Contour: when a grown outline shares a cut level with another outline (for example Top Z with the stock top one stepdown or more over it), the leads no longer cross the other outline, so the post is no longer blocked by a crossing warning.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2677\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
